---
import { SITE_NAME } from "@/lib/site";
import ShowcaseListing from "@/components/site/ShowcaseListing.astro";

const SOURCES = [
  {
    state: "New Jersey",
    rows: [
      {
        what: "Home-improvement contractors",
        source: "NJ Division of Consumer Affairs — HIC registration",
      },
      {
        what: "Licensed trades & professions (electricians, plumbers, dentists, attorneys…)",
        source: "NJ DCA MyLicense verification system",
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    state: "New York",
    rows: [
      {
        what: "Home-improvement contractors in the five boroughs",
        source: "NYC Department of Consumer and Worker Protection",
      },
      {
        what: "Contractors in Nassau, Suffolk, Westchester & Rockland",
        source: "County consumer-affairs licensing offices",
      },
      {
        what: "State-licensed professions",
        source: "NYS Office of the Professions / Department of State",
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    state: "Pennsylvania",
    rows: [
      {
        what: "Home-improvement contractors",
        source: "PA Attorney General — HICPA registration",
      },
      {
        what: "State-licensed professions",
        source: "Pennsylvania Licensing System (PALS)",
      },
    ],
  },
];

const BADGES = [
  {
    label: "License verified",
    tone: "ok",
    body: "We found the business in the official registry named on its listing, and the record was in good standing on the date shown.",
  },
  {
    label: "License not verified",
    tone: "warn",
    body: "The trade requires a license or registration and we could not confirm one, or the business hasn't provided a number yet. Ask before you hire.",
  },
  {
    label: "License not required",
    tone: "neutral",
    body: "No state or county license applies to this category. We still run the identity, review, and responsiveness checks.",
  },
  {
    label: "Suspended",
    tone: "danger",
    body: "The registry shows the license as lapsed, revoked, or suspended. We remove or clearly flag these listings.",
  },
];
---

<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:py-16">
  <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted">Methodology</p>
  <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl font-bold text-ink">How we verify</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-faint">
    Written by the {SITE_NAME} editorial team · Updated August 2026 · AI tools assist with
    drafting; a person reviews every page and makes every verification decision.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Most directories list anyone who signs up. {SITE_NAME} checks. This page explains exactly
    what our badges mean, where our license data comes from, and how listings are ordered — so
    you never have to take our word for it.
  </p>

  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="example-heading">
    <h2 id="example-heading" class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">
      What a verified record looks like
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-5">
      <ShowcaseListing />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="steps-heading">
    <h2 id="steps-heading" class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">
      The four checks, in order
    </h2>
    <ol class="mt-6 space-y-6">
      <li class="rounded-card border border-line bg-surface p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">1 · Identify</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          We confirm the business exists and is who it says it is: a working phone number, a
          real address or defined service area, and a named owner or principal. Businesses we
          can't identify don't get listed at all.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-card border border-line bg-surface p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">2 · Verify the license</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Where a category requires a license or registration, we look the business up in the
          official government registry — not a data broker — and record three things on the
          listing: the license number, the registry we checked, and the date we checked it.
          Badge copy always reads
          <span class="font-mono text-sm">“License verified against {"{source}"} on {"{date}"}”</span>.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-card border border-line bg-surface p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">3 · Check reviews</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          We read reviews across Google, Yelp, and Facebook and look for patterns — recurring
          complaints, dispute handling, consistency over time — not just the average. We show
          ratings with their source and count, and we never edit, reorder, or hide reviews
          based on sentiment or payment.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-card border border-line bg-surface p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">4 · Confirm they're taking work</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted">
          A great business that never answers is a bad recommendation. We confirm each listed
          business is active and reachable, and listings show typical response times once we
          have enough data to report them honestly.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="sources-heading">
    <h2 id="sources-heading" class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">
      Where our license data comes from
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Every verification names its source. These are the official registries we check, by state:
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">
      {SOURCES.map((group) => (
        <div class="rounded-card border border-line bg-surface p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">{group.state}</h3>
          <dl class="mt-3 space-y-3">
            {group.rows.map((row) => (
              <div class="grid gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_1fr] sm:gap-4">
                <dt class="text-sm text-muted">{row.what}</dt>
                <dd class="font-mono text-sm text-ink">{row.source}</dd>
              </div>
            ))}
          </dl>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-faint">
      Registration or licensure confirms a business met a state's registration requirements at
      the time we checked. It is not a government endorsement of the business's competency, and
      it is not a guarantee of work quality.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="badges-heading">
    <h2 id="badges-heading" class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">
      What each badge means
    </h2>
    <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3">
      {BADGES.map((badge) => (
        <li class="flex flex-col gap-2 rounded-card border border-line bg-surface p-5 sm:flex-row sm:gap-5">
          <span
            class:list={[
              "inline-flex h-fit w-fit shrink-0 items-center rounded-chip px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold",
              badge.tone === "ok" && "bg-ok-wash text-ok",
              badge.tone === "warn" && "bg-warn-wash text-warn",
              badge.tone === "danger" && "bg-danger-wash text-danger",
              badge.tone === "neutral" && "bg-inset text-muted",
            ]}
          >
            {badge.label}
          </span>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{badge.body}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="ranking-heading">
    <h2 id="ranking-heading" class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">
      How listings are ordered
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      List pages have two zones, and they never mix:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-4">
      <li class="rounded-card border border-line bg-surface p-5">
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">The featured block — always labeled</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          At most three paid placements can appear at the top of a list page, always marked
          “Featured” or “Sponsored,” with sponsored link attributes for search engines. Paid
          placement is the only thing money buys here.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-card border border-line bg-surface p-5">
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">The organic list — a transparent score</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Everything below the featured block is ordered by a score built from four public
          factors, in this priority: whether the license is verified, how many reviews the
          business has, its rating across platforms, and how recently we re-checked the
          listing. Payment, claimed status, and agency relationships have zero weight.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-faint">
      Businesses that are clients of our agency are always disclosed as sponsored wherever they
      appear. They receive no ranking benefit.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-sm leading-relaxed text-faint">
      Editorial independence, spelled out: clients of the agency that operates this directory
      pay for web and SEO services only — never for placement, scores, badges, or how their
      reviews are handled. Staff never write or edit reviews, for anyone. And agency clients
      are excluded from editorial "best of" selections unless the published, data-driven
      criteria put them there on their own.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="freshness-heading">
    <h2 id="freshness-heading" class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">
      Freshness and corrections
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Verification isn't permanent. Licenses lapse, businesses close, phone numbers change.
      Every listing shows when it was last verified, and re-checks are scheduled — not
      best-effort. If you spot something wrong on any listing, tell us and we'll re-verify it
      against the source registry. See our
      <a href="/editorial-policy" class="font-medium text-brand underline underline-offset-2">editorial policy</a>
      for how corrections work.
    </p>
  </section>
</article>
